For a point (x, y) to lie inside or on the boundary of the rectangle, its x-coordinate has to be at least x1 and at most x2 and its y-coordinate at least y1 and at most y2; the rectangle is closed on all four sides, and the rectangle's edges run along parallel lines x = x1, x = x2, y = y1 and y = y2. The body unpacks the rectangle and iterates through each point with a single combined test, counting those that satisfy both inequalities. The bounds comparison is inclusive, which is why a point on any edge is included in the count. An empty point list produces 0. The code does not assume a particular order on the points or any particular origin.

